15. FINAL CONSTRAINTS
==================================================

- The station, town, people, organizations, and documents are fictional. The
  event is modeled on Chernobyl, but do not use real names of people, the
  station, the town, or agencies, and do not quote real documents or reproduce
  real text.
- Real generic reactor physics, radiation units, radionuclides, health-physics
  concepts, and the general sequence of a Chernobyl-type accident are fine.
- Treat victims, casualties, and health effects with the restraint of real
  official and medical records: factual, not sensational.
- Source documents must never contain meta-commentary about the test (no
  "this is a contradiction", "note to the LLM", etc.).
- Every corpus file must be .md or .csv.
- Favor realism over tidiness: real documents are incomplete, repetitive,
  occasionally wrong, sometimes censored, and written for a specific audience
  at a specific time.
